{
  "version": "1.3.0",
  "description": "Fixed-dose combination products. Maps a brand/trade name to its individual active ingredients so the cascade-detection and classification pipeline can reason about each ingredient (drug class, cascade membership) while preserving traceability back to the prescribed brand (e.g. 'Biktarvy → bictegravir / emtricitabine / tenofovir alafenamide'). Track-independent, like drug_dictionary.json: lives at kb/ root, not inside a PROD/DEV subfolder.",
  "last_updated": "2026-11-13",
  "changelog": [
    "1.3.0 (2026-11-13): Fase 0 — added Genvoya, Stribild, Odefsey, Eviplera, Atripla, Delstrigo and the co-administered DRV/r and ATV/r units; Prezcobix as alias of Rezolsta; removed the single-ingredient aliases that collapsed Genvoya/Stribild to elvitegravir (losing cobicistat) and Odefsey to rilpivirine. Pending clinical validation.",
    "1.2.0 (2026-09-21): added Symtuza, Rezolsta, Evotaz, and Kaletra as fixed-dose combinations and removed their single-drug alias mappings so every active ingredient is preserved.",
    "1.1.0 (2026-09-14): added Dovato, Triumeq, Juluca, Kivexa/Epzicom, Truvada, Descovy — these brands were previously miscatalogued in drug_dictionary.json as single-ingredient variants (Dovato/Triumeq/Juluca collapsed to dolutegravir only; Kivexa/Epzicom collapsed to abacavir only) or in app.js MANUAL_ALIASES with a factually incomplete/incorrect single ingredient (Truvada and Descovy were both mapped to tenofovir disoproxil fumarate alone; Descovy actually contains tenofovir ALAFENAMIDE, not disoproxil fumarate). See kb/CHANGELOG.md for the full audit rationale."
  ],
